<title>ITALY: Prodi says Italy won't ask for EMU delay.</title>
<headline>Prodi says Italy won't ask for EMU delay.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Thursday that Rome will not ask for a delay of European monetary union or easy terms to join the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy will not ask for a delay or easy terms. Italy is in a condition to undergo the test that all European countries have to undergo for the single currency,&quot; he told the Senate in a speech before question time.</p>
<p>Prodi said a Europe without Italy would deny the continent a Mediterranean scope.</p>
<p>He said that if Italy did not take part in the first wave of countries taking part in EMU it would be &quot;extremely difficult to catch up for lost time later.</p>
<p>Prodi has repeated stressed that Italy will pull out all stops in oder to make it into EMU when the single currency is launched in 1999.</p>
</text>
